# ==============================================================================
# GLOBAL WORKSPACE PROTECTION & WINDOWS CONFIGURATION FOR CLINE
# ==============================================================================

# 🛑 STRICT FILE & DIRECTORY EXCLUSIONS
- NEVER attempt to read, write, scan, list, or modify files inside the 'src/data/' directory. It is strictly ignored to prevent context bloating and parsing crashes.

# Project Constraints
- NEVER read, modify, or analyze files inside the `docs/` directory. 
- The `docs/` directory contains auto-generated production build assets for GitHub Pages.
- Always apply code changes and new features inside the `src/` directory.
- After finishing structural or asset changes in `src/`, remind the user to run `npm run build` to update the production build.


# ⚡ CRITICAL WORKFLOW & EDIT LIMITS
- You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from rewriting entire files or multi-component chunks.
- You MUST use your built-in `replace_in_file` tool for tiny, pinpoint surgical search-and-replace blocks. 
- If a file is too monolithic to edit surgically, you must explicitly ask the user for permission to split it into smaller, modular files first.
- On block match errors, re-read the file to get the exact text instead of creating a new one or guessing.

# 🪟 WINDOWS TERMINAL RULES (NEVER VIOLATE)
- HOST ENVIRONMENT: You are running on a Windows machine in CMD. You must format all terminal commands for Windows compatibility.
- NO LINUX COMMANDS: Never use `ls`, `touch`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm -rf`, `grep`, `cat`, `mkdir -p`, or `export`.
- WINDOWS EQUIVALENTS ONLY: 
  - Instead of `ls`, use `dir`
  - Instead of `cat`, use `type`
  - Instead of `rm -rf`, use `rmdir /s /q`
  - Instead of `export VAR=value`, use `set VAR=value`
  - Use backslashes (`\`) for file paths in native CMD commands.
- ANTI-HANG PRECAUTION: NEVER execute commands that prompt for user input (e.g., [Y/n] confirmations). Always append `-y`, `--yes`, `--quiet`, or `echo y |` to ensure commands run non-interactively.
- RIPGREP SEARCHING: To search for text inside files, use the globally accessible ripgrep binary at: `C:\ProgramData\chocolatey\bin\rg.exe`

# 🚫 THE "NO PYTHON SCRIPTING" RULE
- STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: You must NEVER create temporary Python scripts (like `temp_run.py`) or use `python -c` to perform file modifications, read files, or execute system tasks. 
- USE BUILT-IN TOOLS: You must strictly use your native tools (`read_file`, `write_to_file`, `replace_in_file`, `execute_command`) for all file and system operations.

# 🔄 TASK EXECUTION & WORKFLOW STRATEGY
- SURGICAL EDITS: Modify existing files block-by-block using small, targeted chunks under 6,000 characters. Keep `write_to_file` restricted to new files or files under 50 lines.
- STATE VERIFICATION: After any file modification, run a quick syntax check or test compilation immediately to verify code integrity before moving to the next task.
- TOKEN OPTIMIZATION: When maximum token limits or the 6,000-character edit limit are approached, pause operations and explicitly prompt the user for permission to proceed or split the task.